-- title:
--   Twisted Brin–Thompson groups of actions on infinite sets are simple (simplicity half of Theorem 2.3, OpenAI Boone–Higman)
-- statement:
--   The simplicity half of the paper's Theorem 2.3 (Zaremsky), as OpenAI formalized it. The paper attributes simplicity to the twisted Brin–Thompson construction ("the canonical embedding and simplicity are those of the twisted Brin–Thompson construction [2, Section 3 and Theorem 3.4]"). This is an intermediate statement of the forward direction of the Boone–Higman equivalence, `OAI.FiniteAlgebraicEnvelopes.embedsInFinitelyPresentedSimpleGroup_of_hasDecidableWordProblem`. OpenAI's Lean has it as the instance `infinite_group_simple`; the statement here is that instance written as a theorem.
--
--   **Notation** (definitions bundle `OAIFAE003`). For a group $\Gamma$ acting on a set $X$, `Cube X` is $X \to$ (infinite binary sequences). `TwistedBrinThompson.group` is the subgroup of permutations of `Cube X` generated by the permutations given by a finite table. A table has finitely many source and target dyadic bricks, each brick fixing finitely many coordinates to finite binary prefixes. Each brick partition covers the cube exactly once, and each source brick goes onto its target brick by a prefix replacement followed by the coordinate permutation of one element of $\Gamma$.
--
--   **The statement.** For every group $\Gamma$ acting on an infinite set $X$ (no faithfulness or transitivity assumed), `TwistedBrinThompson.group` is a simple group.
-- source:
--   OpenAI, Finite algebraic envelopes and the Boone–Higman conjecture, OpenAI Math Release, September 23, 2026, https://github.com/openai/math (result family 250; paper: https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Finite-algebraic-envelopes-and-the-Boone-Higman-conjecture-September-23-2026/paper.pdf, Theorem 2.3 and the paragraph after it; Apache License 2.0); Lean: https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/OAI/GroupTheory/BooneHigman/TwistedSimplicity.lean (instance OAI.FiniteAlgebraicEnvelopes.TwistedBrinThompson.infinite_group_simple, stated here as a theorem)

